   "line": [
    "Nd7"
   ],
   "spoken": "Now a subtle idea — the knight retreats to d7 to force the strong enemy knight off its central square. It looks like it hangs a pawn, but there's a point: if the pawn is taken, it rips open a file that hands over massive attacking chances.",
   "kind": "plan"
  },
  {
   "ply": 19,
   "t": 132.5,
   "fen": "r2qk2r/pp1n1ppp/2bbp3/2ppN3/5P2/1P1PP3/PBP3PP/RN1Q1RK1 b kq - 0 10",
   "line": [
    "f4"
   ],
   "spoken": "This beats the routine queen move, where the opponent could cement the knight with a pawn to f4. They play the pawn thrust anyway, but now the knight can simply be taken — and the queen gains access to the very square that thrust just opened up.",
   "kind": "tactic"
  },
