   ],
   "spoken": "The winning method is patient improvement — finish development and castle, overprotect the sensitive f7 pawn by swinging the queen back, blunt the long-diagonal bishop with a pawn, and open some air on the kingside with a pawn break. Then, since the opponent has vacated a file, double the rooks on it, centralise the queen, and tuck the king to safety before pushing. Small, purposeful moves, each leaving the position healthier, until the advantage becomes decisive.",
