   "spoken": "The deeper rationale for the sacrifice — the pawn thrust defends the knight and makes it hard to dislodge, so the retreat forces it out, and even if the opponent grabs material and snatches on the fianchetto, a rook to the open file brings a swarm of pieces to bear on the king. A queen move induces a weakness and long castling keeps the attack rolling — it may not be full compensation objectively, but it's the classic time-buying sacrifice, keeping the initiative alive and the position messy.",
